      "name": "bullet3d.rigid_body.apply_force",
      "brief": "Apply a force at a world-space position",
      "description": "This has the same point semantics as <code>b2d.body.apply_force</code>: <code>world_position</code>\nis the point where the force is applied. The binding converts it to the\ncenter-of-mass-relative offset expected by Bullet's <code>applyForce</code> method.",
      "returnvalues": [],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "body",
          "doc": "rigid body",
          "types": ["btRigidBody"],
          "is_optional": "False"
        },
        {
          "name": "force",
          "doc": "force in Defold units",
          "types": ["vector3"],
          "is_optional": "False"
        },
        {
          "name": "world_position",
          "doc": "application point in world space and Defold units",
          "types": ["vector3"],
          "is_optional": "False"
        }
      ],
      "examples": "Apply an upward force at the game object's current world position:\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kr\">function</span> <span class=\"nf\">init</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">self</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"kd\">local</span> <span class=\"n\">body</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">bullet3d</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get_rigid_body</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;#collisionobject&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"kd\">local</span> <span class=\"n\">force</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">vmath</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">vector3</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">bullet3d</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rigid_body</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">apply_force</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">force</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">go</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get_world_position</span><span class=\"p\">())</span>\n<span class=\"kr\">end</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
